# INT-203 — real Coraza log lines, captured from the booted edge tier on
# 3 Sep 2026, unedited apart from this header.
#
# Provenance matters here more than usual, because the point of the fixture is
# that the leak is REAL. These are the lines Traefik wrote when the corpus case
# `sqli_in_turkish_utterance_field` was sent through the deployed middleware
# chain, with one change to the payload: the Turkish clinical sentence was put
# in front of the injection, which is what a patient's field looks like when an
# attacker uses the patient's own field. Read the `data` value: CRS's `logdata`
# quotes the matched ARG back, and on this API that ARG is
# `ARGS:json.text_tr` — the reason a person is seeing a doctor.
#
# tests/infra/test_waf_rules.py asserts that no part of it survives into an
# EdgeEvent, and — the near-miss control — that the rule id, the CRS family and
# the block verdict do.
#
# The last line is Traefik's own startup output: a line this parser must drop
# rather than guess at, because an unparsed line shipped verbatim is the leak.
